                <pb facs="0211" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v09/pg185"/>

                <head>81. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Concerns in the Government of Japan about the Kennedy administration’s proposed interest equalization tax
                    prompted Japanese Foreign Minister Masayoshi Ohira to come to Washington for
                    discussions with senior U.S. officials. He met separately with Under Secretary
                        Ball and Secretary Rusk on August 1 and with President Kennedy on August 2, 1963. Memoranda of all
                    three conversations are scheduled for publication in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1961-63v22">volume XXII</ref>. Regarding earlier Japanese
                    complaints on this question, see <ref target="#d79">Document 79</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
